course: dictionary
lesson: 4740
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Horror can mean a strong feeling of fear and shock, a terrible thing, or a scary film or story. Look at the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «The horrors of war» means terrible, frightening things that happen in a war. «A horror film» means a film made to scare people. The clue is in the words next to horror: war is terrible, and a film is what you watch.
explain: Be careful with the informal meaning. «You little horror!» is a playful way of calling a naughty child a little troublemaker. Nobody is really scared here. Ask yourself: is anyone frightened, or is someone just being cheeky?
fact: Horror means a strong feeling of fear and shock.
fact: «A horror film» and «a horror story» are meant to scare people.
fact: «The horrors of war» means terrible, very frightening things.
fact: «In horror» means feeling shocked and frightened, as in someone staring in horror.
fact: Informally, «You little horror!» is a playful way of saying a naughty child.
exercise: «Kieran picks a horror film rated 15.» In this sentence, what is a horror film? | *A film meant to scare people | A film about cooking | A film with no story | A cartoon for very young children
exercise: Leo says, «You little horror!» Is someone scared here? What does horror mean in this phrase? | A strong feeling of fear | Something very dull | A terrible monster in a cave | *A naughty child, said playfully
exercise: Find and copy the word that means terrible, very frightening things. | rated | film | *horrors | Kieran
test: Which phrase shows someone feeling shocked and frightened? | A cosy cwtch | Very happily | To sleep in peace | *In horror
test: «Connor has nightmares for a week.» Which word in the sentence tells you a horror film is scary? | Mum | week | *nightmares | Connor
exam: In «a horror film», which meaning of horror fits? | A naughty child | A strong feeling of joy | *A kind of film or story meant to scare people | A hot drink
